    {
      "id": "claim_fb6e47d68194461a8bc5d5c7def9519e",
      "statement": "The data path is fenced by stamping the epoch into the replication prefix: a cell replicates to cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/ with plain unconditional PUTs, so a stale owner writes only into a superseded prefix that restores never select.",
