    {
      "id": "claim_3c0620355e83401a9612cb66703342ef",
      "statement": "Memory-pressure shedding publishes least-recently-used idle cells as unowned without resetting their epochs and the shedding node refuses to reacquire unowned cells, so takeover uses the same bucket protocol as ordinary traffic.",
